      "problem": "Factor the expression $9{y}^{5}-{y}^{3}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that all of the terms have a common factor of ${y}^{3}.$ To simplify the computation, we can factor out the ${y}^{3},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n9{y}^{5}-{y}^{3}={y}^{3}(9{y}^{2}-1)\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the expression $9{y}^{2}-1$ using the difference of squares formula:\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}(9{y}^{2}-1)={y}^{3}((3y)^{2}-{1}^{2})={y}^{3}(3y+1)(3y-1)\n$$",
